Project title
EduGenie – Google Gemini Powered Learning Assistant
Requirement Analysis
Requirement Analysis
Requirement analysis defines what EduGenie should do, who will use it, what information it needs, and what constraints the system must satisfy. It converts the ideation-stage concept into clear, implementable system requirements.
________________________________________
1. Project Overview
EduGenie is an AI-powered learning assistant that uses Google Gemini to provide personalized academic assistance to students.
The system is intended to support the complete learning cycle:
Learn → Ask → Practice → Evaluate → Improve
Instead of functioning only as a question-answering chatbot, EduGenie should provide personalized explanations, study resources, quizzes, study planning, and learning recommendations.
________________________________________
2. Problem Statement
Students often have difficulty obtaining personalized academic support outside the classroom. Conventional learning platforms generally provide predefined content and may not adapt explanations according to an individual student's knowledge level.
Students may need to:
•	Understand difficult concepts.
•	Clarify doubts immediately.
•	Summarize lengthy learning materials.
•	Generate practice questions.
•	Prepare for examinations.
•	Create personalized study schedules.
•	Identify weak topics.
•	Revise previously learned concepts.
Therefore, a system is required that can provide interactive, personalized, and AI-assisted learning support.
________________________________________
3. Objectives
The main objectives of EduGenie are:
1.	Provide an AI-based academic assistant.
2.	Answer student questions using natural language.
3.	Explain concepts at different difficulty levels.
4.	Generate summaries and study notes.
5.	Generate quizzes and practice questions.
6.	Create personalized study plans.
7.	Analyze quiz performance.
8.	Identify areas requiring additional revision.
9.	Support learning through uploaded study material.
10.	Provide recommendations based on learning activity.
11.	Provide a simple and accessible user interface.
12.	Use Google Gemini as the primary generative-AI capability.
