7. Functional Requirements
Functional requirements describe what the system must do.
FR-01: User Registration
The system shall allow a new student to create an account.
Required information
•	Name
•	Email/username
•	Password
•	Preferred language
•	Educational level
________________________________________
FR-02: User Authentication
The system shall allow registered users to:
•	Log in.
•	Log out.
•	Maintain an authenticated session.
•	Reset their password where supported.
________________________________________
FR-03: Student Profile
The system shall maintain a basic learning profile containing information such as:
•	Educational level
•	Subjects of interest
•	Preferred language
•	Learning preferences
•	Study goals
Only necessary information should be collected.
________________________________________
8. AI Tutor Requirements
FR-04: Ask Academic Questions
Students shall be able to enter natural-language questions.
Example:
"Explain binary search."
The system sends the relevant prompt/context to Gemini and displays the generated response.
________________________________________
FR-05: Concept Explanation
The system shall provide explanations that can include:
•	Definition
•	Key concepts
•	Examples
•	Step-by-step explanation
•	Real-world analogy
•	Important points
________________________________________
FR-06: Difficulty-Level Selection
The student should be able to request explanations at different levels:
•	Beginner
•	Intermediate
•	Advanced
Example
Topic: Machine Learning
Beginner → simple explanation
Intermediate → technical explanation
Advanced → detailed technical/mathematical explanation
________________________________________
9. Study Material Requirements
FR-07: Summarization
The system shall generate concise summaries from provided learning content.
Possible output:
Original Material
       ↓
AI Processing
       ↓
Summary
       ↓
Key Points
       ↓
Important Terms
________________________________________
FR-08: Notes Generation
EduGenie shall generate structured notes from learning material.
Notes may contain:
•	Headings
•	Definitions
•	Key points
•	Examples
•	Important formulas
•	Revision points
________________________________________
FR-09: Document-Based Question Answering
Where document upload is supported, users should be able to ask questions related to their learning material.
Example:
"What are the three main principles discussed in this chapter?"
The AI response should be grounded in the supplied material where technically supported.
________________________________________
10. Quiz Requirements
FR-10: Quiz Generation
The system shall generate quizzes based on:
•	Subject
•	Topic
•	Difficulty
•	Number of questions
Example:
Subject: Data Structures
Topic: Trees
Difficulty: Intermediate
Questions: 10
________________________________________
FR-11: Multiple Question Types
The system may support:
•	Multiple-choice questions
•	True/False
•	Short-answer questions
•	Application-based questions
________________________________________
FR-12: Quiz Evaluation
After submission, the system shall:
1.	Evaluate supported objective answers.
2.	Calculate the score.
3.	Display correct/incorrect answers.
4.	Provide explanations.
5.	Store the result for progress tracking.
________________________________________
11. Study Planner Requirements
FR-13: Study Plan Generation
The student shall be able to provide:
•	Examination date
•	Subject
•	Topics
•	Available study time
•	Current preparation level
•	Study goal
EduGenie shall generate a structured study plan.
Example
Day 1 → Arrays
Day 2 → Linked Lists
Day 3 → Stacks
Day 4 → Queues
Day 5 → Revision
Day 6 → Practice Test
________________________________________
12. Personalized Learning Requirements
FR-14: Learning History
The system should maintain relevant learning activity such as:
•	Topics studied
•	Quizzes attempted
•	Quiz scores
•	Frequently requested concepts
•	Completed study activities
________________________________________
FR-15: Weak Topic Identification
Based on available performance information, the system should identify topics where additional practice may be useful.
Example:
Revision suggested: Recursion
Recent quiz accuracy: 55%
This should be presented as a learning recommendation rather than an authoritative assessment of the student's ability.
________________________________________
FR-16: Personalized Recommendations
The system should recommend:
•	Topics for revision
•	Practice quizzes
•	Related concepts
•	Additional explanations
•	Revision activities
________________________________________
13. Multilingual Requirements
EduGenie may support multiple languages.
For example:
"Explain photosynthesis in Tamil."
The system should generate an explanation in the selected language while preserving important technical terminology where appropriate.
The initial implementation can begin with:
•	English
•	Tamil
Additional languages can be added later.
