16. Non-Functional Requirements
Non-functional requirements define how well the system should operate.
NFR-01: Performance
The application should provide AI responses within a reasonable response time under normal network and API conditions.
________________________________________
NFR-02: Usability
The interface should be:
•	Simple
•	Intuitive
•	Mobile-friendly
•	Easy for students with limited technical knowledge
A student should be able to ask a question without needing technical instructions.
________________________________________
NFR-03: Availability
The application should be available whenever the underlying application infrastructure and Gemini service are operational.
The system should handle temporary service/API failures gracefully.
________________________________________
NFR-04: Scalability
The architecture should allow the system to support increasing numbers of:
•	Users
•	Conversations
•	Quiz attempts
•	Learning records
•	Study materials
________________________________________
NFR-05: Security
The system should:
•	Protect user credentials.
•	Use secure authentication.
•	Protect API credentials.
•	Restrict unauthorized access.
•	Validate user input.
•	Secure stored learning information.
Gemini API credentials should never be exposed directly in client-side code.
________________________________________
17. Privacy Requirements
Since EduGenie may process student-generated content, privacy should be considered from the beginning.
The system should:
•	Collect only necessary user information.
•	Protect stored user data.
•	Avoid exposing one student's information to another.
•	Provide appropriate account/data deletion mechanisms.
•	Clearly explain how submitted learning content is handled.
•	Avoid storing sensitive information unnecessarily.
________________________________________
18. Reliability Requirements
AI-generated information can occasionally be incorrect.
Therefore, the system should:
•	Avoid presenting uncertain information as guaranteed fact.
•	Encourage verification for important academic information.
•	Provide explanations rather than unexplained answers.
•	Handle API failures.
•	Handle malformed user requests.
•	Provide meaningful error messages.
________________________________________
19. AI-Specific Requirements
FR-19: Gemini Integration
The system shall integrate Google Gemini through an appropriate API/service layer.
Gemini can be used for:
•	Natural-language understanding
•	Content generation
•	Summarization
•	Explanations
•	Quiz generation
•	Conversational interaction
•	Multimodal processing where supported by the selected implementation
________________________________________
FR-20: Prompt Management
The application should use structured prompts to control the AI's educational behavior.
Example conceptual prompt:
You are EduGenie, an educational assistant.

Student level: Beginner
Subject: Computer Science
Topic: Recursion

Explain the concept using:
1. Simple definition
2. Intuitive analogy
3. Example
4. Step-by-step explanation
5. Short practice question

Do not provide unsupported factual claims.
Encourage the learner to understand the reasoning.
________________________________________
20. AI Safety and Academic Integrity
EduGenie should be designed as a learning assistant, not merely an answer-generation tool.
Potential requirements:
•	Encourage students to understand solutions.
•	Provide hints when appropriate.
•	Offer step-by-step reasoning.
•	Support practice instead of facilitating unauthorized examination assistance.
•	Avoid generating harmful or inappropriate educational content.
•	Provide appropriate safeguards for younger users where applicable.
